      "page_title": "Tag vs Digest and Mirrors",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A push uploads missing layer blobs, the config, then the manifest",
            "A pull fetches the manifest, then layers ==in parallel==",
            "Only **missing** layers move: shared base layers are reused"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Tag vs Digest",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Tag",
            "Digest"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Example",
              "`app:1.4.2`",
              "`app@sha256:9f2c…`"
            ],
            [
              "Mutability",
              "{red:mutable pointer}",
              "{green:immutable, exact}"
            ],
            [
              "Deploy use",
              "readable release name",
              "pin for reproducible rollout"
            ],
            [
              "Risk",
              "can be re-pushed",
              "unreadable to humans"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Use immutable version tags like `1.4.2`",
            "Add a **git SHA** tag for traceability to the commit",
            "Never deploy a mutable `latest` to production"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Rate Limits and Mirrors",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Docker Hub ==rate-limits== pulls by anonymous and free users",
            "Fix: authenticated pulls, or pull from a mirror",
            "A **pull-through cache** (registry mirror) keeps pulled layers local",
            "It speeds up CI and eases rate-limit pressure"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Private Registries",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Run `registry:2` for a minimal self-hosted store, or ==Harbor== when you need vulnerability scanning, **RBAC** and replication across sites.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Example: Push to GHCR",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker login ghcr.io",
            "docker tag app:1.0 ghcr.io/acme/app:1.0 && docker push ghcr.io/acme/app:1.0"
          ],
          "note": "push fails unless you tag first"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Store, tag, push, pull"
    },
