    {
      "page_title": "Hardening Containers and Supply Chain",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Why Isolation Is Thin",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Containers share the ==host kernel==, so isolation is weaker than a VM",
            "A **kernel** exploit can escape the container to the host",
            "Root in a container is root on bind-mounted files",
            "Goal: shrink what an escaped process can do"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Run Unprivileged",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Set `USER` in the Dockerfile or `--user` at runtime",
            "==User namespace remapping== maps container root to an unprivileged host user",
            "__Rootless Docker__ runs the daemon itself without root",
            "Drop caps: `--cap-drop ALL`, then `--cap-add` only what is needed",
            "Example: `NET_BIND_SERVICE` lets a non-root app bind port 80"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker run -d --user 1000:1000 \\",
            "  --cap-drop ALL \\",
            "  --cap-add NET_BIND_SERVICE \\",
            "  --read-only --tmpfs /tmp \\",
            "  --security-opt no-new-privileges \\",
            "  myapp:1.4"
          ],
          "note": "--read-only needs tmpfs for writable paths"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Lock the Runtime",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Control",
            "What it does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{green:--read-only}",
              "Root filesystem immutable; tmpfs for writes"
            ],
            [
              "{blue:seccomp}",
              "Filters syscalls; Docker ships a default profile"
            ],
            [
              "{purple:AppArmor / SELinux}",
              "Restricts file and resource access"
            ],
            [
              "{orange:no-new-privileges}",
              "Blocks setuid privilege escalation"
            ],
            [
              "{red:--privileged}",
              "**Never**: all capabilities plus device access"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 4
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Supply Chain Flow",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Pin digest",
                "sub": "base@sha256",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Scan CVEs",
                "sub": "Scout, Trivy, Grype",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "SBOM",
                "sub": "what is inside",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "Sign",
                "sub": "cosign or DCT",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Fail the CI build on ==critical== findings",
            "Prefer minimal __distroless__ base images: fewer packages, fewer CVEs",
            "Secrets: BuildKit secret mounts, Swarm or Compose secrets, or a vault, **not** `ENV`"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Root vs Hardened",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Setup",
            "Escape impact"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Root container",
              "{red:Full host impact}"
            ],
            [
              "Rootless",
              "{green:Unprivileged host user}"
            ],
            [
              "+ caps dropped",
              "{green:Few kernel powers}"
            ],
            [
              "+ read-only fs",
              "{green:Small blast radius}"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3
        }
      ],
      "hero": "shield-check",
      "aside": "least privilege!",
      "subtitle": "Harden and isolate"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Security Mistakes and Audit Checklist",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red",
          "style": "ribbon"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Mounting `/var/run/docker.sock` into a container grants **host control**",
            "Using `--privileged` to silence a permission error",
            "Passing passwords with `ENV` or `-e`: they persist in image history and `inspect`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN --mount=type=secret,id=tok \\",
            "  sh -c 'cat /run/secrets/tok \\",
            "  | npm login --stdin'"
          ],
          "note": "secret never lands in a layer"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Audit Checklist",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Does the image run as ==non-root==?",
            "Is the base pinned by **digest** and scanned in CI?",
            "Are caps dropped and the root fs read-only?"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Spot Escalation",
          "text": "Run `docker inspect --format '{{.HostConfig.Privileged}}' c` to catch a privileged container."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "text": "How do you harden a container? Why is --privileged dangerous? How are secrets handled in builds and runtime? What does rootless mode change?"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "banner",
          "title": "KEY TAKEAWAYS:",
          "text": "Run rootless, drop caps, go read-only, scan and sign, keep secrets out of ENV."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "shield-check",
      "subtitle": "Harden and isolate"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Logs, Exit Codes and Shell Access",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. First Look",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker ps -a` shows state, including exited containers",
            "`docker logs --tail 100 -f` follows the last 100 lines",
            "`docker inspect` returns full JSON: ==state==, exit code, mounts",
            "It also shows networks, env and health in one place",
            "`docker stats` and `docker top` show live CPU, memory, processes"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Exit Codes",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Meaning",
            "Typical cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "{green:0}",
              "Clean exit",
              "PID 1 finished"
            ],
            [
              "{orange:1}",
              "App error",
              "Uncaught exception"
            ],
            [
              "{red:125}",
              "Daemon error",
              "Bad `docker run` flag"
            ],
            [
              "{red:126}",
              "Not executable",
              "Missing +x bit"
            ],
            [
              "{red:127}",
              "Command not found",
              "Wrong path or CMD"
            ],
            [
              "{purple:137}",
              "SIGKILL or OOM",
              "Memory limit hit"
            ],
            [
              "{blue:143}",
              "SIGTERM",
              "`docker stop`"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 4
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Inside the Container",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Need a shell?",
            "rows": [
              [
                "a"
              ],
              [
                "b",
                "c"
              ],
              [
                "d",
                "e"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "a": {
                "text": "docker exec -it c sh",
                "shape": "pill",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              "b": {
                "text": "Shell exists?",
                "shape": "diamond",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              "c": {
                "text": "Distroless, no sh",
                "shape": "box",
