      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Why Orchestrate",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One host cannot give ==scheduling== across machines or **self-healing**",
            "Production adds scaling, rolling updates and service discovery",
            "Secret management must work across every node",
            "An orchestrator keeps the __desired state__ true, always"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Swarm and Kubernetes",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{icon:docker} ==Swarm== is built in: `docker swarm init`",
            "Swarm objects: services, replicas, overlay network",
            "{icon:kubernetes} ==Kubernetes== is the industry standard",
            "K8s objects: pods, deployments, services, ingress",
            "Huge ecosystem makes K8s the default choice"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Scope",
            "Trade-off"
          ],
          "rows": [
