    {
      "page_title": "Logs, Shutdown and Safe Deploys",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Logs, State, Shutdown",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Send stdout/stderr to a ==log driver==: json-file, fluentd, loki, awslogs",
            "json-file needs `max-size` and `max-file` rotation",
            "Stay ==stateless==: keep state in volumes, databases or object storage",
            "Handle **SIGTERM** and set `stop_grace_period` to drain connections"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Drain Before Kill",
          "text": "After the grace period expires, Docker sends SIGKILL, so size `stop_grace_period` to your slowest request."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Deploy Safely",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deploy by ==immutable tag== or digest, never a moving tag",
            "Use rolling or blue-green updates",
            "Keep a rollback path: the previous image stays available"
          ],
          "style": "star"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Swarm Rollback",
          "text": "Run `docker service rollback web` to return a service to its previous spec."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**No log rotation** on json-file fills the disk and takes the host down",
            "Fix: set `max-size` and `max-file` in the log options"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
